{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And they came to Marah, etc.</b> One needs to know why sometimes He calls it מָרָתָה [Maratah] and sometimes מָרָה [Marah]. And it appears that the name of the place was מָרָתָה [Maratah], and the spring of water that was in it did not have a distinct name." "And it says <b>and they could not drink water from Marah</b> — meaning, from the spring that was in Maratah, because they are bitter. Afterward the verse turns back to reveal to you that the name Marah that it mentioned is a name that was fixed for that spring after they found its waters bitter; Scripture called it by the name of the future. And according to this approach, its saying <b>for they are bitter</b> is precisely correct, since the naming Marah is for the future, and at that point it was not yet called by the name Marah — it is as though it said ״to drink water from Maratah.״ Therefore it needed to say <b>for they are bitter</b>. And understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:30.468053499Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}